meta {
  name: List with running balance
  type: http
  seq: 2
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/transactions?accountId=acc_chequing&sort=-date&withRunningBalance=true&pageSize=50
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

params:query {
  accountId: acc_chequing
  sort: -date
  withRunningBalance: true
  pageSize: 50
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  The one derived per-row value the server offers. It requires **exactly one**
  `accountId` and a date sort (`400` otherwise): a running balance across
  several accounts has no meaning, and one out of date order is not a balance.
  
  It is computed over the account's whole ledger, not the filtered page — a
  cumulative figure that ignored hidden rows would be wrong. Pending rows get
  `null`, because an unsettled row has no defensible total.
}
